
## Web

- Use Bun: `bun add <package>` (`--dev` for tools), and commit `bun.lock`;
  never npm, which would add a `package-lock.json`. `bun run dev` starts
  the dev server. A version must be 3 days old before Bun installs it
  (`bunfig.toml`), and packages' install scripts don't run unless the
  package is in `trustedDependencies` or on Bun's own vetted list; add a
  package there only when it can't work without its script. `make check`
  fails on a high or critical advisory (`bun audit`); `bun audit fix`
  updates to a safe version.
- Code lives in `src/`, with tests next to the code as `*.test.tsx`.
- Keep quant and data logic in a Python service, not in the browser.
